DXQuant's metadata declares AGPL-3.0-or-later. The complete version 3 license text
is included in LICENSE.txt from the frozen DX reference; license wording
is unchanged (trailing blank lines are normalized).
Copyright notices in source files are retained.

DXQuant is inspired by and partly ports DX Analytics:
https://github.com/yhilpisch/dx
The frozen legacy checkout is not bundled. DXQuant is a partial rewrite with
explicitly different numerical/API contracts; it does not claim clean-room
provenance or complete legacy equivalence.

Well-known numerical formulas were implemented and checked against analytical
identities and synthetic benchmarks. QuantLib 1.44 was used locally to compute
synthetic SABR, CIR, and Heston test fixtures. QuantLib itself is not bundled.
Runtime dependencies retain their own licenses and are installed separately.

Research, structuring, drafting, and visualizations were assisted by different
LLMs as co-writing tools under human direction.
